Infocom (R.I.P, alas) always used to have a section in their hint books
with the above title, which would tell you some of the things you could
do in an Infocom game that would generate funny or unexpected messages
(such as WALK AROUND THE BULLDOZER twice in _Hitchhiker's Guide_, or
PUT BAG IN BAG in most games, or...).

Clearly NetHack is is dire need of this kind of list.  The reason I
bring this up is because of a side note from a nearby thread:

+-- snelling@bmerh466.bnr.ca (Peter Snelling) writes:
| TUTTI_FRUTTI has to
| be the most intricate totally useless feature in nethack.
| 
| Granted, it does produce the funniest message in the game (when you 
| rename your favorite fruit 100 times to 100 different things), but
| this checking for plurals boggles my mind.


I looked at this, said "you've got to be kidding," tried it -- and
there really is a message that pops up after the 100th time you've
renamed your favorite fruit.

So, what else is there?  Have you ever tried:
  * applying a leash to yourself
  * praying while hallucinating
  * applying a mirror to a nymph
  * ?

Is there a list like this already out there that I don't know about?


